# C33 — API Client, Test Cases and the calls panel

Phase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C32.

## Outcome

API Client and Test Cases render in the new shell with immutable response history, a live completion status, and the "Show the calls" panel reusing the response renderer.

## Inputs and dependency gates

C32; screens/api-client-test-cases.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),
[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).
Read the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its
companions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is
an immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.

## Milestones

1. API Client re-skin; `role="status"` completion region; history snapshots unchanged by later configuration (I5).
2. Test Cases re-skin with pack-sourced cases from the wizard; Runtime-only "Open in Playground" hand-off and "Inspect" for every other product, which never dispatches a scan (V2-T15, P21).
3. `show_calls` preference and side panel showing redacted request/response from diagnostics.
4. Fixtures for R2Api and R2Cases.

## Required acceptance

- V2-R05, V2-T05, T14, T15, T16; known gap 5 closed; T09 for both screens; non-Runtime rows never dispatch a scan intent (mock runtime assertion).

## Evidence and completion

As C28.

## Safety and recovery

Fixtures only.
# C12 — Case Library and Runtime Home/Inbox observations

Phase: P03. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C11.

## Outcome

Preserve authored cases and truthful Runtime source summaries.

## Inputs and dependency gates

C11; supported case formats, scan execution and Runtime observation contracts.

Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),
[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).
Concrete interfaces follow accepted G01 ADRs. Read the [selected design](../../architecture/DESIGN.md),
[qualification contract](../../architecture/qualification.md) and this chunk's
exact target in [checks.json](../../architecture/checks.json). Freeze all source/shared dependency
inputs; active neighboring worktrees and unavailable methods cannot count as pins.

## Milestones

1. Implement five-product case authoring/specifications, starters, protected save and explicit import/export/catalog import.
2. Only Runtime cases execute through Playground; other types remain inspectable specifications.
3. Implement Runtime Home/Inbox attention/freshness/partial/unknown states and charts without fabricating zero or completeness.
4. Prepare real shared observation presentation for Gateway data added in C18; no placeholder can count as Gateway parity.

## Required acceptance

- Any changed UI also requires T09 actual native keyboard/focus/accessibility checks; global requirements are not deferred solely to C24.

- T01,T06,T08,T13,T19: case limits/conflicts/import errors, unknown case type, unsupported execution and expected verdict.
- Expired/incomplete/failed source remains distinct from healthy empty; attention follows source evidence.
- Native create/save/import/open-in-Playground and scoped Home/Inbox navigation; no Academy XP outside Academy.

G01/C01 must bind these assertions to exact commands and fixture/native targets
before execution. Run appropriate regressions when changes reach earlier chunks.
No test result, native acceptance, or live qualification is claimed by this file.

## Evidence and completion

T23 is mandatory here for this feature's local work and reconnect behavior: offline launch/read/edit, explicit retry, preserved uncertain outcomes, and no replay of pending reviews/scans/inference/HTTP mutations/tool calls. C24 repeats the cumulative matrix.

Case compatibility/execution table, source-state tests and native Library/Runtime observation receipts.

Use the [implementer prompt](../prompts/implement-chunk.md) and
[independent reviewer prompt](../prompts/review-chunk.md). Require ≥9/10 overall
and in architecture, behavior, authority/security, and validation; no required
fixes or absent mandatory evidence. Preserve attempts, raw verdicts, hashes, and
remediation. Commit only the reviewed tree; do not unlock the next chunk early.

## Safety and recovery

Explicit public catalog imports use approved fixture/catalog snapshots during development. No implicit cloud upload of saved cases.
