Rules: an unavailable product or tab never produces a verification result, an
Inbox item, an inventory row or a review. The wizard's verify step lists it
as "Not available" (not pass, warning or fail). Test V2-T19 asserts that the
admin inventory for an unavailable product has no tabs and no actions, and
V2-R10 asserts that no intent exists that would mutate it; V2-T20 and V2-R11
cover unavailable tabs and denied actions within admitted products.

## 7. Error presentation

- **Refusal** (core refused an intent): warn toast with the refusal reason and
  the tenant named; never a modal. Guard-type refusals (tenant switch with a
  pending decision) render their dialog from the refusal payload.
- **Delivery unknown**: inline "not confirmed" state on the control that
  dispatched, with Retry; the control is not reset.
- **Contract violation**: generic warn toast; detail to diagnostics.

## 8. Accessibility additions

The native acceptance checklist gains four items that every P09 chunk's
acceptance script asserts: accent-colour focus ring on every focusable
control (inset variant where declared); `role="status"` live regions for read
status, API send completion and review apply; one topmost modal with
`aria-hidden` siblings and focus return; toasts persist under Reduce Motion.
Existing requirements (keyboard-only, VoiceOver attributes, 150%/200% zoom,
contrast AA) continue to apply to every changed screen.

## 9. Budgets

Existing `budgets.json` entries carry unchanged. New: a tenant switch renders
the new tenant's Home from cached scopes within 100 ms, with read status
showing pending until the read lands (measured by the C30 workload).

## 10. Known gaps carried from the prototype

Codex round 16 (score 8) left five items, closed by the chunk named:

1. Secret disclosure survives a tenant switch with the key review open → I6, C31.
2. Applied injection-override examples show "Not demonstrated" → topic
   verdicts keyed separately from detectors, profile-aware, C31.
3. Administration creation labels from a per-product single value → per-tab
   `AdminInventory` capability and label, C31.
4. Home snooze tooltip hard-codes "Snooze 24 hours" → shared item
   `snoozeLabel`, I11, C30.
5. API Client Send announces nothing → `role="status"` completion region, C33.

## 11. Verification

- Behaviour: Vitest + Testing Library component tests, one named fixture per
  prototype wrapper board; the board → initial props → test id table is in
  [screens/boards.md](screens/boards.md), so reviewed-state coverage can be
  audited without reconstructing canvas wrappers.
- Contract: Rust integration tests per invariant (`V2-Rxx`).
- Native: the existing Accessibility-API scripts, extended per chunk, plus a
  screenshot evidence set per chunk at 100% and 200% zoom in both themes filed
  under `evidence/Cxx/screens/`.
- Live: only C29 (wizard verify against Vulture, reads only) and C31 (review
  apply against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix) run live, inside the
  scope the owner designated on 2026-10-25. Every other chunk runs on fixtures
  and the mock runtime.
- Review: C27 at 9/10 in every dimension, enforced by the controller (a
  `docs_only` chunk refuses owner acceptance and needs no native
  preparation); C28–C34 may complete at 8 under D034 and are raised to 9
  before the P09 phase review.
- Legacy native scripts removed in C34 are first mapped, assertion by
  assertion, to replacement native-check ids (C34 milestone 2), so the
  cumulative P09 gate keeps exercising every earlier authority and
  accessibility requirement.
# Native acceptance procedure (T09 and chunk native assertions)

`xtask native --chunk Cxx` builds the fixture-identity app with
`native-prepare` and records its executable SHA-256. Acceptance is a separate
record, `docs/planning/evidence/Cxx/native-acceptance.json`
(schema `airs-v2/native-acceptance/1`, parsed strictly by xtask), produced by
actually driving that exact executable:

- `method: "cua"` — automation through macOS accessibility/automation APIs
  against the real native window (for example REA native UI capture or System
  Events), with the captured accessibility trees/screenshots stored under
  `evidence/Cxx/native/`; or
- `method: "operator"` — a person performs the checklist on the real app and
  records observations per check.

Every check must report `pass` with an observation and evidence paths. A
`fail` or `blocked` check, a record naming different executable bytes, or a
record for the production identity fails the gate. Build success, mocked IPC
tests or reviewer scores never substitute for this record.

Prerequisites on the acceptance host: macOS grants the automation client
**Accessibility** (to read the AX tree and send key events) and, for
screenshots, **Screen Recording**. Without these grants automated acceptance is
blocked; the operator method remains available.

## Required checks

The authoritative per-chunk check list is
[native-checks.json](native-checks.json) (`airs-v2/native-checks/1`). xtask
requires the record to contain exactly those IDs, once each, with result
`pass`, a nonempty observation and at least one evidence file that the review
packet hash-binds; the record must name the fixture identity and the prepared
executable, whose current bytes are re-hashed at completion. Changing the list
is a reviewed source change (it is part of the build-flags fingerprint).

C01 covers launch/identity, native menus, keyboard-only navigation and focus,
the palette (including native navigation while it is open), unavailable
destinations, Rust-owned appearance, the accessibility tree, minimum window
size, zoom to 150%/200%, Reduce Motion, absence of Academy gamification, and
startup network behavior.

VoiceOver: C01-N08 inspects the accessibility attributes VoiceOver consumes
(AXRole, AXTitle/AXDescription, AXValue/selected state and element order) and
records exactly which were read. Spoken VoiceOver output is not claimed by an
attribute inspection; it is recorded only when an operator actually runs
VoiceOver, and otherwise remains a C24 cumulative item.
# Tokens

The desktop app owns its appearance. A local token file
(`apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css`, created in C28) defines these names as
CSS custom properties under `--v2-*`, with the light values on `:root` and the
dark values under `[data-theme="dark"]`. Academy's `--academy-*` variables are
left intact for the embedded learner view; where a shared Academy component
renders inside the new shell, the Academy variable it reads is aliased to the
`--v2-*` value in the shell's scope only. No colour is written inline in a
component.

## Colour (from `L` and `D` in `prototype/R2App.dc.html` line 677–678)

| Token | Light | Dark | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| bg | #f6f2e9 | #1d2021 | Page background (body gets this explicitly) |
| side | #ebe5d8 | #161919 | Sidebar and wizard rail |
| paper | #fbf8f1 | #282828 | Cards, dialogs, sheets |
| inset | #efe9dd | #32302f | Selected row, inset panels, explain track |
| rule | #e0d9ca | #3c3836 | Borders between regions, secondary buttons |
| ctl | #857d6e | #8a7f70 | Control borders (inputs, selects, toggles) — AA against bg and paper |
| ink | #14141a | #ebdbb2 | Primary text |
| soft | #4a463c | #d5c4a1 | Secondary text |
| faint | #635d50 | #bdae93 | Tertiary text, meta lines — still AA at 12px on bg |
| acc | #a33d15 | #fe8019 | Accent: primary buttons, focus ring, selected sidebar item |
| accInk | #ffffff | #1d2021 | Text on accent |
| accSoft | #f4dfd3 | #4a2f1a | Accent tint backgrounds |
| block | #b42318 | #ff6b57 | Verdict Blocked, Critical severity |
| blockBg | #fbe4e1 | #3d1f1c | Blocked background |
| flag | #8a5300 | #fabd2f | Verdict Flagged, Warning severity |
| flagBg | #faeed5 | #3a3019 | Flagged background |
| ok | #1f6f3a | #b8bb26 | Verdict Allowed, success |
| okBg | #def0e3 | #2b2f17 | Success background |
| sel / selInk | = acc / accInk | = acc / accInk | Selected tenant in the switcher |
| get | #245e8f | #83a598 | HTTP method and link colour in the API Client |

Verdicts and severities are never colour alone: every use pairs the colour with
an icon and a word (invariant I9).

## Spacing, type and size

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| page-margin-top | 32px | Every destination's top margin |
| page-margin-x | 44px | Every destination's side margin (wizard main: 34/44/24 add-mode, 32/44/28 first-run) |
| title | 26px / 700 | Destination and wizard step titles |
| card-pad | 18–20px | Card and dialog inner padding |
| gap | 10–12px | Between controls and cards; inner card gap 12px |
| text | 14px | Body |
| text-2 | 12px | Secondary text. 11px only for pills, eyebrows and mono badges |
| control-h | 32px | Inputs, selects, buttons |
| radius | 7px controls, 12px cards | |
| rail-w | 244px | Sidebar and add-tenant wizard rail (first-run wizard rail 320px) |
| reading-max | 860px | Reading width cap for prose and forms |
| focus | 2px solid acc, offset 2px; `data-inset-focus` buttons use offset −4px | Visible focus everywhere |
| window-min | 1180×720 | Rail collapses to icons below 1280 wide; no horizontal scroll anywhere |

## Theme switching

Theme remains Rust-owned (`setAppearance`). The shell sets `data-theme` on the
document root from the observed appearance and `prefers-color-scheme` for
"system". Tokens are the only place a theme value lives.
